sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Worker A
    participant B as Worker B
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Catalog advisory (65102, 2): protects price_versions, not a column
    A->>D: SELECT oldest pending candidate outside a transaction
    B->>D: SELECT the same candidate outside a transaction
    A->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
    B->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
    Note over B,D: WAIT, A owns the customer account
    A->>D: Shared catalog lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Recheck pending state
    alt A completes or quarantines the usage_inbox row
        A->>D: COMMIT processed_at and financial writes<br/>Or processing_error with no financial effect
        D-->>B: Account lock granted
        B->>D: Shared catalog lock, reload pending usage_inbox row
        D-->>B: No pending row for this identity
        B->>D: COMMIT without financial writes
    else A fails before commit
        A->>D: ROLLBACK every financial and completion write
        D-->>B: Account lock granted
        B->>D: Shared catalog lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>usage_inbox row is still pending
        B->>D: Account once and COMMIT
    end
    Note over A,D: Same-customer usage_inbox rows also serialize when identities differ.<br/>Different accounts can rate concurrently under shared catalog locks.
